bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_lowering_error_names_entry_file_not_defining_module_2026-11-26, 0, "A lowering type error raised inside an IMPORTED module is reported against the ENTRY file. Repro: m2a.spl = use m2b.{z} + main; m2b.spl = pub fn z() -> text: d.get(\"k\") on a Dict<text, text>. compile m2a.spl prints: declared return type mismatch in function z (m2a.spl) ... and compile failed (m2a.spl). The function line (function at line N / return at line N) then points into the wrong file. During the sweep the defining file had to be found with strace (std.sys.env get resolved to src/compiler_rust/lib/std/src/sys/env.spl:17). Expected: the message names the defining module path. eprintln site: src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/hir/lower/module_lowering/function.rs (self.current_file is the entry file while imported functions lower)."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_lowering_error_names_entry_file_not_defining_module_2026-11-26, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "Lowering type error in an imported module names the entry file - SEED patch implemented (body_diagnostic_file prefers flattener owner attribute; 3 files) pending seed rebuild; pure-Simple lane verified correct by construction; spec 4/4 PASS 2026-11-27", not the defining module", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/hir/lower/module_lowering/function.rs, 1, simple compile m2a.spl -o /dev/null (m2a imports z from m2b), 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_lowering_error_names_entry_file_not_defining_module_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-26 filed from the same sweep (Fable review note); reproduced on the seed (fix6)."
    seed_lowering_error_names_entry_file_not_defining_module_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: reproduced on fresh HEAD seed (explicit and implicit return variants; run lane identical). Root cause: pipeline/module_loader.rs flattens imports into one module so Lowerer current_file stays the entry path for all lowered functions; the flattener already tags imported fns with __simple_flatten_module_owner__ and lower_function reads it into current_function_owner, but the return-type diagnostics read current_file + line-only spans (stmt_lowering.rs:1098-1104, function.rs:1524-1540, plus outer wrappers naming the entry unit). Fix (patch-only, no build): new pub(super) body_diagnostic_file() in hir/lower/lowerer.rs (owner attr beats current_file, same policy as record_private_ref); the explicit-return wrap, implicit-return wrap and eprintln now name it. Pure-Simple lane attributes correctly by construction (per-module lowering, driver keys receipts by module path) - proven in-process: inferring the imported module yields exactly 1 error keyed under its own path with line 2; the clean entry yields 0. New spec test/01_unit/compiler/type_inference/imported_return_type_mismatch_names_defining_module_spec.spl 4/4 PASS. Post-rebuild acceptance: compile m2a/m3a name m2b/m3b inside the parenthetical and eprintln; entry functions byte-identical (owner attr absent -> current_file fallback); E1003 tags unchanged so existing specs stay green. Residual: outer wrappers still name the compiled entry unit around the corrected inner verdict (cosmetic; needs a file/position channel on LowerError - follow-up); argument-slot rejects and hoisted nested fns of imported modules not covered (no regression, follow-up sweep). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/type_inference/imported_return_type_mismatch_names_defining_module_spec.spl prevention=test/02_integration/app/diagnostics/check_optional_return_into_scalar_spec.spl"

